        "original_id": "c5381320-dbe7-5eed-93cf-f042c35c5f4f",
        "text": "This chunk describes Karamay, Meihekou, and Baijiantan District.\n\nThis chunk is about:\n- Places: Karamay, Meihekou, Baijiantan District, Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region, People's Republic of China\n- Topics: administrative jurisdiction, transport infrastructure\n\nFacts:\n- Karamay, also called Kelamayi, is a prefecture-level city in the north of the Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region in the People's Republic of China.\n- Meihekou is a regional transport hub that connects three single-track railway lines and two national highways.\n- Baijiantan District is a district in the Xinjiang Uyghur Autonomous Region that is under the administrative jurisdiction of Karamay City.",
